    "answer": {
      "short": "Step 2 cancels $\\sin x$, losing $x=0^\\circ,180^\\circ,360^\\circ$. The complete solutions are $x=0^\\circ,60^\\circ,180^\\circ,300^\\circ,360^\\circ$.\n\nFactorise instead of cancelling.",
      "worked": "Step 2 divides by $\\sin x$ without retaining the case $\\sin x=0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}2\\sin x\\cos x&=\\sin x\\\\2\\sin x\\cos x-\\sin x&=0\\\\\\sin x(2\\cos x-1)&=0\\end{align*}$$\n\nEither $\\sin x=0$, giving $x=0^\\circ,180^\\circ,360^\\circ$, or $2\\cos x-1=0$, giving $x=60^\\circ,300^\\circ$.\n\nTherefore $x=0^\\circ,60^\\circ,180^\\circ,300^\\circ,360^\\circ$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
